<BaseLayout title="Living with MS" description="Access starts with listening."><article class="prose"><header class="page-hero"><a href="/advocacy/">← Advocacy</a><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:18px">Starter draft · awaiting Beth’s personal edit</p><h1>Living with MS</h1><p class="intro">Access starts with listening.</p></header><p>A person should not have to make an invisible struggle visible before being taken seriously. Living with MS deserves room for honesty, changed plans, and support without an interrogation.</p><p>Ask what helps. Believe the answer. Make it easier to rest, participate, or say “not today” without guilt. Accessibility is not a prize for pushing through.</p><p>This space is for the everyday side of living with MS: dignity, practical access, and being seen as a whole person. Personal stories will come in Beth’s own words.</p></article></BaseLayout>
